<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Additional Implementation Details</h3>

<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Fine-tuning setup.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unless otherwise specified, we follow the official training configurations of the original model implementations, while using half of each LIBERO dataset for fine-tuning and reserving the other half as non-member data; the number of training steps is correspondingly reduced to half of the official configuration.
For OpenVLA, we use LoRA with rank <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>32</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32</annotation></semantics></math>, learning rate <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>, image augmentation enabled, and a shuffle buffer size of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math>k, trained on <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> A100 GPUs with per-GPU batch size <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math> and gradient accumulation <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> for an effective batch size of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>128</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">128</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>-FAST, we apply LoRA on the PaliGemma backbone with rank <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math> and learning rate <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>, trained on <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> A100 GPUs with effective batch size <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>32</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0.5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0.5}</annotation></semantics></math>, we apply LoRA on both the PaliGemma backbone (rank <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math>) and the action expert (rank <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>32</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32</annotation></semantics></math>), with learning rate <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>, trained on <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> A100 GPUs with effective batch size <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>32</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32</annotation></semantics></math>.
All effective batch sizes match the official settings of the corresponding models.</p>
</div>
